  "beats": [
    {
      "t": "2026-11-17T00:00:01Z",
      "text": "In November 2026, Namit Malhotra confirmed the postponement, saying the filmmakers needed more time to complete the film given its scale.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1386581821:179"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-17T00:00:08Z",
      "text": "Critics have given the film mixed-to-positive reviews.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1386581821:9"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-17T00:00:15Z",
      "text": "Ramayana: Part 1 is a 2026 Indian Hindi-language epic mythological film directed by Nitesh Tiwari, who co-wrote the screenplay with Shridhar Raghavan.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1386581821:0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-17T00:00:24Z",
      "text": "Ramayana: Part 1 stars Ranbir Kapoor, Yash, Sai Pallavi and Ravi Dubey; with music by Hans Zimmer and A. R. Rahman.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:box:1386581821:starring",
        "wiki:box:1386581821:music"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-17T00:00:33Z",
      "text": "Released: 27 October 2026 (Academy Museum), 5 November 2026 (India). Box office, as Wikipedia records it: ₹1481.91 crore.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:box:1386581821:released",
        "wiki:box:1386581821:box-office"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-17T00:00:43Z",
      "text": "On 30 April 2024, the second schedule commenced in Mumbai.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:film:1386581821:6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-17T00:00:51Z",
      "text": "The article places the filming in Film City, Ayodhya and Mumbai.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:film:1386581821:1",
        "wiki:film:1386581821:2",
        "wiki:film:1386581821:6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-17T00:01:01Z",
      "text": "Birthplaces are on record for 5 of the people credited, and 4 of them were born in India.",
      "cites": [
        "wd:Q108560:P19",
        "wd:Q16908467:P19",
        "wd:Q20081051:P19",
        "wd:Q7296622:P19",
        "wd:Q76364:P19"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-17T00:01:09Z",
      "text": "Hans Zimmer was born further afield, in Frankfurt, Germany.",
      "cites": [
        "wd:Q76364:P19"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-17T00:01:19Z",
      "text": "On 17 November 2026, 452,299 people read the English article, about 34 times the usual daily count.",
      "cites": [
        "views:en:Ramayana:_Part_1:2026-11-17",
        "views:en:Ramayana:_Part_1:prior"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-17T00:01:26Z",
      "text": "The article is read in 10 languages; after English, the most readers were in Hindi, with 1,662.",
      "cites": [
        "views:en:Ramayana:_Part_1:2026-11-17",
        "views:hi:रामायणम्_(2026_फिल्म):2026-11-17"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-17T00:01:33Z",
      "text": "Each language glows where it is mainly spoken, brighter for more readers, and a language is not a country.",
      "cites": [
        "views:hi:रामायणम्_(2026_फिल्म):2026-11-17",
